:false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1201,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":7608,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","cpp","database","distributed-database","distributed-sql","distributed-sql-database","high-performance","kubernetes","multi-cloud","multi-region","scale-out","sql"],"visibility":"public","forks":1201,"open_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-15713](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-15713)\n### Description\n\n* `core.c` and `make_join_rel.c` in `pg_hint_plan` consist of copies of the functions from `src/backend/optimizer/path/allpaths.c` and `src/backend/optimizer/path/joinrels.c` with some of the functions called from there patched up to redirect to the pg_hint_plan counterparts to augment shortcomings of the standard extension hooks.\n* Inconsistency between those copies and the originals leads to obscure inconsistent behavior with hinted queries.  (Example: #25108)\n* In order to keep them in sync, `pg_hint_plan/core.c` and `pg_hint_plan/make_join_rel.c` should be generated from their original source using a perl script: `pg_hint_plan/update_copied_funcs.pl` as a part of the build process.\n* The original [pg_hint_plan/update_copied_funcs.pl](src/postgres/third-party-extensions/pg_hint_plan/update_copied_funcs.pl) tires to extract the source file path from the `postgres` binary found in the command search path (specified by `$PATH` environment variable, `$path` shell variable, etc.) using the `objdump` command as show below:\n ```\nopen (my $in, '-|', \"objdump -W `which postgres`\") || die \"failed to objdump\";\nwhile (<$in>)\n{\n\tif (/DW_AT_comp_dir .*: (.*\\/)src\\/backend\\//)\n\t{\n\t\t$srcpath = $1;\n\t\tlast;\n\t}\n}\nclose($in);\n\ndie \"source path not found\" if (! defined $srcpath);\n#printf(\"Source path = %s\\n\", $srcpath);\n```\n* However, this approach has the following problems, and the perl variable `$srcpath` should be specified via build system or operating system environment variable instead.\n  1. The `postgres` binary in the command search path may not be built from the source tree that `pg_hint_plan` extension is being built for.\n  2. The 'objdump' command is platform (OS and the C compiler toolchain) specific.  In fact, the command option '-W' does not work on macOS.  Wouldn't work with clang on Linux, either.\n  3. The source file names could have been stripped off of the binary.\n\n### Issue Type\n\nkind/enhancement\n\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\n\n- [x] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\n\n[DB-15713]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-15713?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/26360/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/26360/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"mtakahar","id":8877300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NzczMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8877300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar","html_url":"https://github.com/mtakahar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"http