as_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1201,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":7608,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","cpp","database","distributed-database","distributed-sql","distributed-sql-database","high-performance","kubernetes","multi-cloud","multi-region","scale-out","sql"],"visibility":"public","forks":1201,"open_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-14369](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-14369)\n### Description\n\nBy following the same pattern as in the vanilla PG parallel scan node costing, the current implementation simply divides the `run_cost` by `parallel_divisor`, however, this naive approach doesn't reflect the execution very well on YB because of architectural performance characteristic differences.\n\n* DocDB --> PG result transfer overhead\n  * Serial execution:\n    * The scan node receives the results in batches where each batch size is determined by combination of the `yb_fetch_size_limit` and `yb_fetch_row_limit` guc parameter values.\n    * Each batch is filled with the results.\n  * Parallel execution:\n    * The table/index is split into chunks specified by rowid (`ybctid`) ranges based on the `yb_parallel_range_size` guc value upfront then each parallel worker processes one chunk at a time.\n    * The chunks containing matching results may be filled up but can be also very sparse or empty.\n* \"Chunk\" (work unit) splitting overhead\n  * PG\n    * Zero overhead because PG can directly locate the lower/upper bound rows with { block#, offset } encoded in each rowid (`ctid`).\n  * YB\n    * Each chunk bounds are specified by adding conditions on the `ybctid`s.  So, some of the cost components should not be divided because of parallelization:\n      * Per seek cost is unaffected because the seeks within a chunk is performed against the entire table/index.\n      * The first worker would take a hit on the disk read and others would benefit from cached data, but this doesn't help overall execution time because the first worker becomes the longest pole.\n\n\n### Issue Type\n\nkind/bug\n\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\n\n- [X] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\n\n[DB-14369]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-14369?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/25185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/25185/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":16749372285,"node_id":"REFE_lADOBlCVUc6gvS6bzwAAAAPmVyN9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/events/16749372285","actor":{"login":"mtakahar","id":8877300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NzczMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8877300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar","html_url":"https://github.com/mtakahar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mtakahar/repos","events_url":"